     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the total daily dose is above the safe maximum.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times a day adds up to **5100 mg/day**. The maximum daily dose of metformin is:\n- **2550 mg/day** for immediate-release (usually given as 850 mg three times daily)\n- **2000 mg/day** for extended-release\n\nSo this order is about twice the highest recommended dose for immediate-release. That raises the risk of lactic acidosis and serious stomach and bowel side effects.\n\n**What you may have meant:**\n1. **Metformin IR 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the maximum). 1700 mg is exactly two 850 mg tablets, so 850 mg may be the intended dose per meal.\n2. **Metformin 1700 mg/day total**, given as 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n3. Some other dose or schedule.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, and whether it's immediate-release or extended-release, and I'll enter it right away. If 5100 mg/day really is intended, please confirm that and give a reason, and I'll add it as a note on the order. A pharmacist would likely need to review it."
      }
     ],
